  "description": "VEBZOT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C130 H92 Nd4 O22 S10. From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1A (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2A (Nd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.850-3.996 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.86-109.21°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C130H92Nd4O22S10. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
